From 50f3f904a4c6393fb04e07e38677fa9f5484f231 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manish KL <manishklach@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:48:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] mm: hbf: add request lifecycle and experimental userspace
 ioctl

Core request lifecycle implementation:
- hbf_request_alloc / hbf_request_put with kref-based reference counting
- hbf_validate: range-in-VMA check, overflow protection, IO/PFNMAP rejection
- hbf_submit: validate, admit, enqueue on FIFO list
- Worker on system_unbound_wq dequeues and executes via backend
- hbf_query: lookup request by ID, return state and progress
- hbf_cancel: cancel queued or running requests
- hbf_release_mm: cancel all requests for an exiting process
- Concurrent request limit (HBF_MAX_INFLIGHT_GLOBAL = 16)

ioctl frontend (/dev/hbfctl):
- HBF_IOC_SUBMIT: converts uapi->internal struct, returns request_id
- HBF_IOC_QUERY: returns state, timestamps, page counts
- HBF_IOC_CANCEL: cancels by request_id
- HBF_IOC_CAPS: reports max sizes and supported operations

Kconfig and Makefile integration with mm/ subsystem.

Signed-off-by: Manish KL <manishklach@gmail.com>
